1 INTRODUCTION
In recent years, driver assistance systems have undergone significant development. It is predicted that in the next decades, sensor technology and information processing capacity will advance to a level that allows highly (SAE Level 4) [17], and even fully automated driving (SAE Level 5) [14]. At these levels, driver intervention is no longer required, which means the best possible user experience and comfort for passengers, who can use the time during the journey for activities such as working or sleeping [20]. It also ensures greater safety in the long term by preventing traffic accidents, and fatalities caused by human error [7, 21]. However, automated driving is accompanied by multiple human factors and challenges, such as loss of the passenger’s situation awareness or the basic challenge of establishing trust in the automated vehicle [13]. Transparency and

