Figure 3: Procedure of the study
We chose a within-subject design for the experiment. Thus, each participant experienced all three concepts in randomized order. The procedure of the study is shown in Fig. 3. In the beginning, participants were informed about the background and procedure of the study and gave informed consent. The study itself started by filling in a demographic questionnaire that also included questions about the participant’s experience with automated driving functions and their usage behavior in regard to their own vehicle. Before the 360° videos of the concepts were presented to the participants through the VR headset, a generic video was shown to help familiarize them with the VR environment and the study setup. After each concept, the participants were instructed to evaluate the concepts by filling in the STS-AD and SIPA questionnaires. In the second part of the study, a semi-standardized interview was conducted. The whole study lasted about 30-40 minutes.
4.4 Sample
We recruited 24 participants (14 male, 10 female; age range 16 to 49 years, M = 24.54, SD = 7.33). 12 of our participants were students, 6 were employed and one was not employed. All participants owned a driver’s license and participated voluntarily in the study without receiving any compensation.

