5.1.1 Trust in Automation. The effect on trust (Fig. 4, left) was analyzed using a repeated measures ANOVA. For all analyses, the level of significance was set at 𝛼 = .05. The calculations were conducted using R. The results show that the concept had a significant effect on situational trust, F(2,23) = 9.456, p < .001. The post-hoc t-test show that trust in automation is significantly different between concept A (no additional information, M=3.799, SD=1.281) and concept C (highest amount of information, M=4.632, SD=1.064) (p < .001), while there was no significant difference between concept A and concept B (additional information regarding the ego-vehicle, M=4.160, SD=1.128) (p = .39). There was also a significant difference between concept B and concept C (p = .01). All p-values were adjusted using the Bonferroni method.
